The project will be developed in four stages:

Stage 1 – System Design

Define healthcare energy requirements.

Identify essential and non-essential loads.

Develop system architecture.

Stage 2 – Hardware Development

Integrate solar panel and battery.

Connect sensors and microcontroller.

Develop low-voltage demonstration setup.

Stage 3 – Software Development

Implement energy monitoring.

Develop priority-control logic.

Create monitoring interface.

Stage 4 – Testing and Validation

Test energy monitoring accuracy.

Evaluate priority switching.

Measure response time and system performance.
